Z||000007||deceler8||12-03-2001||05:33 PM||||I re-did my shift console in oak mainly because I couldn't find another one in good condition that I was willing to pay for.<P>Since my car doesn't have power windows, I was able to remove the filler panel that blocks the opening in the shift console plate and rout some new ashtray doors and the filler out of oak.<P>I made a cup holder insert that goes far enough down into the console area that it will hold a fairly large cup easily without tipping. The insert also has a bottom on it so the cup won't go down too far.<P>I also have a solid piece that fits in the same area which I attached my garage door opener to hide it from prying eyes.<P>The picture is a side view in poor light (need new batteries in the digital).<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dec03$02.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/deceler8_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
